The user wants me to implement a FIFO (First-In-First-Out) queue in Structured Text (ST) for PLC programming. Let me analyze the requirements:

1. Capacity is 8
2. Input buttons trigger only on rising edge (low to high), and holding doesn't repeat
3. Initial count=0, queue empty, both button histories are initially FALSE
4. popEn rising edge executes first (dequeue): if not empty, remove first item; if empty, no change
5. pushEn rising edge executes after pop (enqueue): if count<8, append pushItem to logical tail; otherwise reject
6. When full queue has both in and out, first remove one slot then add
7. When empty queue has both in and out, only new item remains
8. Output: count = current length, full = count=8, empty = count=0
9. head = 0 when empty, otherwise head = first item
10. fifo is caller's bound array, readable/writable during execution, at end of each cycle fifo[1..count] is compact logical queue

